# Clients implementing embedded Relate may build this as a named context
# (--build-context relate=../relate). Allowlist: the leading `*` excludes
# everything (.git, docs, fixtures, build output, …) and the `!` lines
# re-include exactly what cargo needs: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and every
# workspace group: relate/*, surfaces/*, testing/*, extensions/*
# (the CLI links relate-wire through relate-mcp — ADR-0431 §11,
# R3). A new top-level workspace group MUST be re-included here or every
# Docker build that compiles the CLI breaks (observed: the first
# create-loadtest-baselines run after extensions/ landed failed on the
# missing extensions/relate-wire/Cargo.toml). New NON-workspace
# top-level dirs stay excluded by default. dockerignore is
# last-match-wins,
# so a later line re-excludes the Python sources (pyo3 builds happen
# outside Docker; maturin pulls in a large tree). Nested `.venv`,
# `node_modules`, and `target` directories inside the re-included
# trees are excluded after that.
# .cargo/config.toml only sets wasm32 rustflags and rust-toolchain.toml
# is only honored by rustup (absent from rust:1.88-alpine), so neither
# is re-included.
#
# One docs file is compile-time input, not documentation for the reader:
# the CLI pins the extension kit's canonical body with include_str! at
# build time (surfaces/relate-cli/src/extensions/kit.rs), so the
# memory-shape image — which builds `--bin relate` — needs it in the
# context. Re-include exactly that file via the parent-chain pattern
# (dockerignore cannot re-include under an excluded parent, so each
# ancestor is re-included first and its other children re-excluded); the
# rest of docs/ stays excluded.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!relate
!surfaces
!testing
!extensions
surfaces/*/python
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/target
!docs
docs/*
!docs/api
docs/api/*
!docs/api/extensions
docs/api/extensions/*
!docs/api/extensions/examples
docs/api/extensions/examples/*
!docs/api/extensions/examples/mcp-client.sh
# ADR-0251 §5 prebuilt path: `make docker DOCKER_PREBUILT_DIR=<dir>` stages
# the static binaries in target/docker-prebuilt/ and builds with
# --build-arg BINARY_SOURCE=prebuilt. Re-include exactly that directory
# (dockerignore cannot re-include under an excluded parent, so the root
# target/ dir is re-included first and everything else under it stays
# excluded).
!target
target/*
!target/docker-prebuilt
# scripts/github-download.sh is the authenticated GitHub release GET
# the chef stage uses for sccache. Re-include that one file; the rest
# of scripts/ stays out of the context.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/github-download.sh
